<title>USA: Bath Iron Works in Maine plans to hire 100 workers.</title>
<headline>Bath Iron Works in Maine plans to hire 100 workers.</headline>
<dateline>BATH 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bath Iron Works in Maine, the state's largest private employer, plans to hire over 100 new workers just a week after announcing it would layoff almost 200 people who work as drafters and fill management slots.</p>
<p>The company said the new hires are needed to fill a number of yard positions, like electricians and painters to keep shipbuilding on schedule.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
